Z||000006||Greg Piet||05-17-2000||09:07 AM||||OK Ill admit I got sucked into K+N land.<P>My reason was becsue at a rallycross (dry lake bed racing), a Fram air filter let some silt into teh motor requiring a rebuild.  So, I did the next one with an oil soaked K+N which did the job.<P>I cant tell any HP gain, but it kept my cars engine from death||||reg||1
Z||000007||BlackGT||05-17-2000||09:31 AM||||Sorry Guys no K&N sticker on my car but yeah<BR>the filter works across the entire RPM range.<BR>Yes it`s a standard rebuild with about 13k miles. 1FST2M6 has someone who will custom bend an exhaust system for me so that will be the next upgrade along with adding cradle<BR>bushings and finally getting around to installing my swaybars which have been collecting dust for some time now. Getting back to the stickers.....I kind of like not<BR>having them there so I can catch moostangs<BR>sleeping...... advertising kinda takes the surprise out of it for me. The only stickers<BR>I`ll have will be small "Engineered Performance" stickers in the corner of the door windows near the sail panels.<P> ||||reg||6
Z||000009||1FST2M6||05-17-2000||11:14 AM||||BlackGT,<BR>optimum shift is between 4700 and 5300 no need to go higher you'll just be sucking wind. (thats what Ed said this morning) Sorry we didn't have grey stickers for ya... we'll be making some soon.. i'll be sure you get a few.  <BR>||||reg||1
