Z||000011||ezsurf||05-17-2000||04:30 PM||||1FST2M6,<BR>Was the car you dyno tested an automatic?  Also, was the previous air filter element paper or foam?||||reg||5
Z||000012||ka4nkf||05-17-2000||09:45 PM||||Try It without a filter and you won't see any difference. this should tell you something.||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||05-17-2000||10:47 PM||||What he said. run it w/o a filter. run it with a couple diferant brand new paper ones. (A six month old filter has significant dirt in it.)<P>Untill K&N satisfactorally answers some questions, I'd never use them. K&N filters have been shown to increase top end wear in a number of applications. By their own admission they don't filter their best untill they've picked up some dirt. <P>If I go to anything other than OEM, I'll move to Amsoil oiled foam. Oiled foam filters have proven reliability and filtering. Why do you think hundreds of thousands of Briggs & Stratton engines use them. These filters will flow near their full capacity untill the hold more dirt than you'd ever think posible. Oiled Foam has more filtering capacity than any other type except an oil bath filter. (Oil bath filters are used only in big trucking and heavy construction equipment. They did use them in cars once uppon a time, but they are just too big and heavy.||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||05-18-2000||08:27 AM||||With the dyno numbers there was an increase. Yeah i heard about the top end wear issue also. but you would think that an OLD nasty paper filter all full of pollen, and such would restrict the flow more than it did. or the K&N really isn't worth the expense if your just looking for HP numbers.. unless you have more cubes than we do. the $30 for the filter will pay for itself in 2 years. (after buying 4 normal paper filters) The filter we took out was a WIX paper filter. The Oil foam filters are ok but they filter even less than the K&N. yes they do flow better. Engineered Performance is a distributor for Amsoil (In my Alfa, my Fiero and the girlfriends Saturn (all K&N adorned)) And the K&N oil is very similar to the foams coating with less weight. (like you said)And the Briggs motors all go to K&N filters when in race application. (my Kart, Jr. Dragsters etc.)  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||05-18-2000||08:29 AM||||oh yeah the car was/is an 86 GT 4spd. Owned by Todd Green (BlackGT)||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cooter||05-18-2000||07:50 PM||||On the Briggs race engines I built, with the K-N filter, after a night of dirt oval racing, the carb's were full of dust! Lots of flow, very little filtering.||||reg||1
